    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The president’s campaign slogan was “Gobernar es educar,” reflecting his belief that governing equals teaching.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Aguirre_Cerda",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "As president, he prioritized education, creating thousands of new regular schools and expanding university access nationwide.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Aguirre_Cerda",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Pedro Aguirre Cerda founded the Production Development Corporation (CORFO) in 1939 to spur import‑substitution industrialization after a devastating earthquake.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Aguirre_Cerda",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "CORFO’s subsidies helped launch Chile’s steel, manufacturing, and sugar industries, laying the groundwork for modern industrial growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedro_Aguirre_Cerda",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
